 "response": "**Getosti's budget is now $2095K.**\n\n**Method**\n- Under the policy, only Finance Office records change the budget. Messages from Facilities, PMO, Sales, Engineering, Operations, Legal, Marketing and Vendor were ignored.\n- A withdrawn update counts as if it never happened. Withdrawals can themselves be withdrawn, so I resolved each chain from its last, unwithdrawn link backward.\n- I then started from the $1730K base in #0001. I applied every Finance Office increase and decrease that was still in effect, once each, in record order.\n\n**Key withdrawal chains**\n- #0002 (+$472K) applies. The chain is #0161 \u2192 #0081 \u2192 #0032 \u2192 #0015 \u2192 #0009 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0002. That leaves #0161, #0032 and #0009 in effect, so #0007 is cancelled.\n- #0003 (+$547K) is withdrawn. #1164 cancels #0154, which leaves #0021 in effect, which cancels #0013, which leaves #0012 in effect.\n- #0006 (+$27K) is withdrawn. #0776 cancels #0037, which leaves #0019 in effect.\n- #0071 (+$436K) applies. #1250 cancels #0150, which leaves #0087 in effect, which cancels #0080.\n- #0049 (+$138K) applies. #1386 cancels #1375.\n- The other chains were resolved the same way. One of them is #0033 (\u2212$259K), which is withdrawn through #1438 \u2192 #0784 \u2192 #0708 \u2192 #0534 \u2192 #0165.\n\nAfter applying all updates still in effect, the running total ends at **$2095K** after #1590.\n\nI did not re-check this total by a second, independent method.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
